{
  "$schema": "../../SCHEMA.json",
  "id": "wp-midnight-admin",
  "name": "深夜の管理者",
  "category": "Challenge",
  "status": "draft",
  "visibility": "public",
  "difficulty": 3,
  "estimatedDuration": "45 分",
  "shortDescription": "デザイン事務所 「さくらデザイン」 の WordPress サイトを引き継いだ翌朝、監視ツールから 「見覚えのない管理者アカウントが夜間に増えた」 という通知が届いた。 攻撃するのではなく、外から見える手がかりだけで 「誰が・どうやって・何を残したか」 を突き止めよう。",
  "instructions": "Fixture wp-midnight-admin: .instructions. Synthetic narrative for platform contract tests.",
  "description": "Fixture wp-midnight-admin: .description. Synthetic narrative for platform contract tests.",
  "writeup": "Fixture wp-midnight-admin: .writeup. Synthetic narrative for platform contract tests.",
  "tags": [
    "wordpress",
    "incident-response",
    "account-compromise",
    "log-analysis",
    "operations",
    "local-play",
    "container",
    "multi-verify"
  ],
  "exposedPorts": [
    {
      "port": 18080,
      "name": "Web (WordPress site)"
    },
    {
      "port": 18081,
      "name": "/verify (loopback scorer)"
    }
  ],
  "learningGoals": [
    "予期しない管理者アカウントがインシデントの最重要シグナルであることを、 実際の環境で体感できるようになる",
    "WordPress が REST API で利用者一覧を外部公開しうること・ アクセスログからブルートフォースと成功ログインを読み分けられること・ 入っているプラグインを棚卸しできることを、 自分で確かめられるようになる",
    "コードを触らずにできる是正 (アカウント削除・資格情報のローテーション・MFA / 最小権限・不要プラグインの削除・利用者一覧の公開制限) を説明できるようになる"
  ],
  "i18n": {
    "en": {
      "name": "The Midnight Admin",
      "shortDescription": "Fixture wp-midnight-admin: .i18n.en.shortDescription. Synthetic narrative for platform contract tests.",
      "instructions": "Fixture wp-midnight-admin: .i18n.en.instructions. Synthetic narrative for platform contract tests.",
      "description": "Fixture wp-midnight-admin: .i18n.en.description. Synthetic narrative for platform contract tests.",
      "writeup": "Fixture wp-midnight-admin: .i18n.en.writeup. Synthetic narrative for platform contract tests.",
      "learningGoals": [
        "Feel, in a real environment, that an unexpected administrator account is a top incident signal",
        "Confirm, yourself, that WordPress can expose the user list through the REST API, that you can tell a brute-force burst from the one successful login in an access log, and that you can take inventory of the installed plugins",
        "Be able to explain the code-free fixes — delete the account, rotate credentials, MFA / least privilege, remove abandoned plugins, and restrict the public user listing"
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "id": "rogue-admin",
          "label": "The admin nobody added",
          "hints": [
            {
              "id": "rogue-admin-1",
              "content": "Fixture wp-midnight-admin: .i18n.en.checks.0.hints.0.content. Synthetic narrative for platform contract tests."
            },
            {
              "id": "rogue-admin-2",
              "content": "Fixture wp-midnight-admin: .i18n.en.checks.0.hints.1.content. Synthetic narrative for platform contract tests."
            },
            {
              "id": "rogue-admin-3",
              "content": "Fixture wp-midnight-admin: .i18n.en.checks.0.hints.2.content. Synthetic narrative for platform contract tests."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "login-trail",
          "label": "How they got in",
          "hints": [
            {
              "id": "login-trail-1",
              "content": "After WHO comes HOW they got in. The intruder came in from somewhere. If you can read the record of access the server keeps (a log), you'll see a wall of failures and one success."
            },
            {
              "id": "login-trail-2",
              "content": "Fixture wp-midnight-admin: .i18n.en.checks.1.hints.1.content. Synthetic narrative for platform contract tests."
            },
            {
              "id": "login-trail-3",
              "content": "Fixture wp-midnight-admin: .i18n.en.checks.1.hints.2.content. Synthetic narrative for platform contract tests."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "orphan-plugin",
          "label": "The plugin left to rot",
          "hints": [
            {
              "id": "orphan-plugin-1",
              "content": "Fixture wp-midnight-admin: .i18n.en.checks.2.hints.0.content. Synthetic narrative for platform contract tests."
            },
            {
              "id": "orphan-plugin-2",
              "content": "A WordPress plugin exposes a description file at `/wp-content/plugins/<name>/readme.txt`. Its `Stable tag` and `Tested up to` lines tell you how long ago its updates stopped."
            },
            {
              "id": "orphan-plugin-3",
              "content": "Fixture wp-midnight-admin: .i18n.en.checks.2.hints.2.content. Synthetic narrative for platform contract tests."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "spam-post",
          "label": "A post you never wrote",
          "hints": [
            {
              "id": "spam-post-1",
              "content": "The last question is WHAT the intruder did. Whoever hijacks an admin usually leaves a trace — a post, a link. Look over the published posts and check whether you wrote each one."
            },
            {
              "id": "spam-post-2",
              "content": "Fixture wp-midnight-admin: .i18n.en.checks.3.hints.1.content. Synthetic narrative for platform contract tests."
            },
            {
              "id": "spam-post-3",
              "content": "Fixture wp-midnight-admin: .i18n.en.checks.3.hints.2.content. Synthetic narrative for platform contract tests."
